  body: |
    # ESA support component in the source

    ## Authored interpretation

    The source states that both ESA(Cont) and ESA(IR) can attract the support component, which is based on the claimant’s entitlement rather than a couple rate or the partner’s circumstances.

    ## Scope and boundaries

    DMG 44631–44632 require the capability and phase conditions to be considered separately. This concept does not calculate a component or transfer its rules to UC or New Style ESA.

    ## Inspected source passages

    - [DMG 44631, PDF page 117](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a68db52229c578debc1a7a3/dmg-v-8-ch-44.pdf#page=117)
    - [DMG 44632, PDF page 117](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a68db52229c578debc1a7a3/dmg-v-8-ch-44.pdf#page=117)
    - [DMG 42612, PDF page 81](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e5ff8a8c9f882ae5997f4c/dmgch42.pdf#page=81)

    ## Evidence and review status

    This is an unreviewed, model-assisted interpretation of selected passages in the frozen DWP guidance. It is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule. ESA(Cont), ESA(IR), New Style ESA, UC and Pension Credit are not equated. The captured source contains historical, transitional and potentially superseded provisions; no complete or current legal rule set is claimed. Machine extraction can affect reading order, footnotes and characters. No visual PDF review or specialist acceptance is claimed.

    Source captured: 2026-09-15T19:45:29.100396Z. This is an acquisition time, not a publication, revision or commencement date. Source-stated dates retain their own role and precision.

